    "background_story": "Mina was a brilliant and ambitious surgeon who had always been drawn to the most challenging cases. During a humanitarian mission in a war-torn country, she was severely injured in a bombing attack. Despite the efforts of her colleagues, Mina's left leg was too badly damaged to be saved, and the difficult decision was made to amputate it. The loss was devastating, but Mina was determined not to let it define her. She underwent rigorous rehabilitation and learned to adapt to her new prosthetic limb. Upon her return to the hospital, Mina continued to practice medicine, using her experience to improve the care of amputee patients. Her own trauma had given her a unique perspective, and she became a leading expert in prosthetic surgery, helping countless others to regain their mobility and independence.",
